cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use legal-ai-agent in your research, product, or policy work, please cite it as below."
title: "legal-ai-agent: glass-box contract review with provenance-anchored citations"
abstract: >-
  legal-ai-agent is an open-source FastAPI service, powered by Claude Opus 4.8, that
  reviews contracts, appeals, and legal documents and returns a structured analysis —
  extracted clauses, risk flags, compliance flags, recommendations, a deterministic
  0-100 safety score with an A-F letter grade, and a glass-box 0-100 overall-confidence
  score. Every finding must attach a verbatim text excerpt from the source; the server
  anchors each excerpt to source by exact substring match and auto-downgrades any
  finding whose citation is not present character-for-character. The model proposes;
  the server verifies at the source level, which makes hallucinated findings
  structurally impossible to score well.
authors:
